    {
      "id": "F-4",
      "claim": "Test conventions in demo-repo/tests/unit/test_applicants.py: the file starts with `from __future__ import annotations`, then `import pytest`, `from loanflow.applicants import Applicant, Business` and `from loanflow.errors import ValidationError`. Tests are module-level functions named test_<entity>_rejects_<condition> or test_valid_<entity>_constructs, each annotated `-> None`. Rejection tests wrap a single keyword-argument constructor call in `with pytest.raises(ValidationError):`. Business tests use business_id='BZ-000456' and legal_name='Rivera Bakery LLC'. The three existing Business tests are test_valid_business_constructs (lines 24-26), test_business_rejects_empty_legal_name (lines 29-31) and test_business_rejects_negative_years_in_operation (lines 34-36). The file has no parametrize decorators and no fixtures.",
