    },
    {
      "id": "F-12",
      "claim": "Vault notes 'Harness Run Summaries/run-summary-run-20261001-obsidianlive-003.md' (the Applicant years_employed guard) and 'Harness Run Summaries/run-summary-run-20261001-obsidianlive-002.md' (the late_fee_tier days_past_due guard) are STALE as records of this checkout's state. The changes they describe are absent. They remain useful as context-only precedent for the pattern, which the current idiom (F-3) still supports. Run -003's verdict was inconclusive because no test covered the default value 0. That is a precedent signal: an existing test already passes years_in_operation=0 (test_applicants.py:31), but only for the empty-legal_name case.",
      "classification": "inferred",
      "supporting_finding_ids": [
        "F-7",
        "F-8",
        "F-3",
        "F-4"
      ],
      "reasoning": "F-7 shows Applicant.__post_init__ and test_applicants.py lack the guard and the regression test that run summary -003 says were added. F-8 shows classify_late_fee_tier lacks the guard that run summary -002 says was added. So both summaries describe states this checkout does not contain, which makes them stale and not contradicted-by-design. F-3 shows the idiom they cite still exists, so their precedent value as context holds."
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Per the Architect role, this artifact does not include the implementation itself: the failing regression test and the guard in Business.__post_init__ belong to node N-IMPLEMENT and are outside the Architect's scope.",
    "Why the vault run summaries for run-20261001-obsidianlive-002/-003 describe changes that are not in this checkout is outside what the repository can show. Possible explanations include a different branch or worktree, or reverted changes. Git history was not inspected because the Architect has no Git tool. The summaries are recorded as stale, not resolved in the vault's favour.",
    "Run -003 was inconclusive because no test exercised the default value (0). This scope's acceptance criteria do not mention the years_in_operation default, so whether the verifier needs a default-value test is a scope question, not a research one."
  ]
